On Wed, 14 Feb 2001, Elrond wrote:
>My Lojban:
>
>     pa djine tefi'e zu'o turni ko'a goi roda
>.i   pa djine tefi'e zu'o facki ra
>.i   pa djine tefi'e zu'o vizbei ko'a
>.ije ne'i le manku tefi'e ralte ra
>
>Perhaps the [goi roda] could be dropped.
>
>Comments ?

I'd drop {ko'a goi}; then at least {ko'a} has an expressed antecedent, even
though it isn't explicitly assigned to it. If you drop {goi roda}, the {ko'a}
means "him" and you don't know whom.

{facki ra} isn't right; the x2 of facki is that which is found out about
something. {tolcri} would make more sense.

